# =============================================================================
# .amlignore -- what NOT to upload to Azure when you submit a job
# =============================================================================
# Every `az ml job create` ZIPS UP your code folder and uploads it. Without this
# file you would send the .venv folder to Azure on EVERY SINGLE RUN.
# On this project that is a MEASURED 1.3 GB -- per submit.
#
# Same idea as .dockerignore in Part 8, and it matters for the same reasons:
#   SPEED    -- uploads take seconds instead of minutes
#   MONEY    -- you pay for storage of every snapshot
#   SECURITY -- conf/local/credentials.yml must never leave your machine
#
# If .amlignore is absent, Azure ML falls back to .gitignore.
# Copy this file into house-price/ before submitting a job.
# =============================================================================

# Virtual environments -- huge, and full of Windows binaries that are useless
# on the Linux machine that will run the job.
.venv/
venv/

# Python leftovers
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# SECRETS -- keep conf/local/ dir so Kedro can find it, but block credentials
conf/local/credentials*
conf/local/*.key
conf/local/*.pem

.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.yml

# Local data and models. The job regenerates these, and Azure stores its own
# copies as job outputs.
data/
!data/01_raw/.gitkeep

# Local noise
.git/
notebooks/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.viz/
.telemetry
drift_report.html
